WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.070
-The President held
yet another rally

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.138
where people were packed
close together,

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:07.874
despite
the coronavirus pandemic,

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.241
after telling his supporters

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:11.010
that virtually nobody
is affected

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.713
by a disease that has killed
at least 200,000 Americans.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:16.082
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.887
The President has been
traveling the country,

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:24.490
holding big rallies with people
packed closely together,

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.926
often without masks,
and putting Americans in danger

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.762
in order to make himself
feel better.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:30.864
And remember,
viruses get passed on,

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.899
so he's potentially
exposing people

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:36.135
who aren't even at his rallies
to the spread of coronavirus,

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:39.071
all because the adoration
of his fans soothes his ego.

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:40.573
Just a tip, if you're a cashier

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.876
at the Chick-fil-A closest
to the rally venue,

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.611
you might consider dressing
like the bad guys from "E.T."

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:47.046
By the way,
this isn't hypothetical.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.282
We already know his rally
in Tulsa

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.083
led to a surge in cases there.

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:53.219
At this point, Trump rallies
are on the list

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.687
of high-risk activities,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.957 line:0%
just like doorknob licking,
hugging everyone on the subway,

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.159 line:0%
and eating shrimp
at the strip club buffet.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:03.162 line:0%
And I'm not even really sure
what rally attendees

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:05.465
are getting out of it for all
the risks they're taking.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.200
I mean, you can't even
really follow

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.468
what the guy is saying.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.603
Most of the time, he just stands
there sweating profusely

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.872
and complaining about things
he recently watched on TV.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:16.442
His rallies are like karaoke
night at the concussion ward.

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.277
You could safely get
the same experience

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:20.179
FaceTiming with your uncle
who lives in Boca

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:22.948
and eats dinner every night
at 4:30 at Red Lobster.

00:01:22.948 --> 00:01:24.250
[ As Trump ]
You have to get there early

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.118
so they don't run out
of the Cheddar Bay Biscuits.

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:29.188
We love -- We love the
Cheddar Bay, don't we, folks?

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:32.291
[ Normal voice ]
For example, Trump often tells
two kinds of fake stories,

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:35.528
stories about going home to
his wife, Melania, after rallies

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.263
and stories about generals

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.832
and other people who come up
to him and call him "sir."

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.901
Obviously, all these stories
are made up.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.102
But even Trump seems
to have trouble

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:44.404
keeping track of his bull[bleep]

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:47.740
because yesterday at his rally
in Pennsylvania,

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.041
he mixed them up.

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:52.078
-Last night, now, I went home,
and I tell you this.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.179
I go home all the time.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.714
"First Lady,
how'd you like the crowd?"

00:01:55.714 --> 00:02:00.386
"Sir, I didn't see it.
I didn't see it.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.288
But I didn't see it, Donald.
I didn't see it."

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.124
Sometimes she'll call me
Mr. President,

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:06.658
but she's only kidding,
believe me.

00:02:06.658 --> 00:02:09.862
-Your wife calls you, sir?
Are you married to Marcie?

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:11.730
And if so, Marcie,
what are you doing?

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.366
Stop pretending to be something
we all know you're not.

00:02:14.366 --> 00:02:16.102
While I can enjoy Trump
forgetting he was telling

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.637
a fake Melania story and
slipping into a "sir" story,

00:02:18.637 --> 00:02:19.939
I do wish it was
the other way around.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.407
Chances are most people
at a Trump rally

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.442
think a wife should call
her husband "sir,"

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:24.844
but none of them would be okay

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.746
if a general called you
"darling."

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:30.382
[ As Trump ] This general came
up to me, big guy, tough guy,

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:32.718
hands like frying pans,
and he took me by the shoulders

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:34.420
and said, "Darling,
you were great tonight."

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.756
And then give me
the tiniest kiss.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.558
Tiniest kiss on the lips,
a pair of butterfly wings.

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:41.760
Why is blood coming out
of everyone's ears?

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.662
[ Normal voice ]
The truth is, Melania
doesn't call you anything.

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:45.264
Not "sir," not "Mr. President."

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.534
Maybe "you again."

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:49.502
I doubt they've spoken at all
during the last four years,

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.337
except for maybe that one time
they were leaving

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.674
the White House
and he pointed at a puddle.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.476
Doesn't do anything for her,
just points at the puddle.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:58.677
Did your marriage
counselor recommend

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.413
finding things you both
have in common?

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.981
[ As Trump ] Oh, look water.
Melania like water.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.049
I've seen her drink water.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.551
You know what?
I'll point at it.

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.185
Point at it
so she doesn't miss it.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:07.653
You know, it's hard to believe,
just yesterday

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:10.422
that was Frosty the Snowman,
tragic loss.

00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:11.790
Tragic loss of Frosty.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.160
But it is
my constitutional right

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.895
to appoint a replacement
for Frosty.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.464
And I'm happy to announce
that our newest addition

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:22.435
to beloved Christmas mascots
is [bleep] bird, the penguin.

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:27.306
[ Normal voice ]
That's the first time I'm
putting eyes on [bleep] bird,

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:28.540
and I feel like
the graphics department

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.276
did a really nice job.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.478
So Trump says that
his wife calls him "sir."

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:35.815
But sure, Joe Biden is the one
in cognitive decline.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.950
I've never heard Biden
make a mistake like that.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.286
And the one time he did mix up
his wife and his sister,

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.021
he immediately
corrected himself.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:44.790
-By the way, this is my
little sister, Valerie,

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.158
and I'm Jill's husband.

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:48.427
Oh, no, this is Val.
Val, you switched on me.

00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:50.696
This is my wife.
This is my sister.

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:52.198
They switched on me.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:55.401
-I mean, sure, it would be ideal
if it hadn't happened at all,

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.703
but if that had been Trump,

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.103
he would have insisted
he was right.

00:03:58.103 --> 00:03:59.137
[ As Trump ]
Why are you laughing?

00:03:59.137 --> 00:04:00.907
This is my wife, Melania.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.675
[ As Pence ]
Sir, I am the vice president.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:03.809
[ As Trump ]
Come here, Melania.

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:06.078
Let me give you a kiss.

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:07.579
Oh, Melania's icy tonight.

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:08.881
[ Normal voice ]
And the Melania story mix-up

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.950
was still probably
the most coherent thing he said.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.186
A weird dynamic has developed
with Trump

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:16.922
where he routinely says
some of the most depraved,

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:18.991
authoritarian things
a president has ever uttered.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:22.328
And as a nation, we mostly just
let him pass by without comment.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:25.498
We treat him like a guy handing
out leaflets on the subway.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.466
I wouldn't be surprised
if at the first debate,

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:29.201
Joe Biden just put in earbuds

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:31.103
and started playing "Minecraft"
on his phone.

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:34.140
For example, on Monday
at another -- excuse me --

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.709
one of his coronavirus
cough-athons in Ohio.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.444
Trump told his supporters
that virtually nobody

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:41.013
is affected by the coronavirus
as the total number of deaths

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:43.282
in the U.S. hit 200,000.

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:45.251
-It affects elderly people,

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:49.455
elderly people with heart
problems and other problems.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.124
If they have other problems,
that's what it really affects.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.426
That's it.
You know, in some states,

00:04:54.426 --> 00:04:57.663
thousands of people,
nobody young.

00:04:57.663 --> 00:05:00.967
Below the age of 18,
like nobody.

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.734
They have a strong
immune system.

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:04.470
Who knows? You look --

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.071
You take your hat off
to the young

00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:08.307
because they have a hell
of an immune system,

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:11.176
but it affects virtually nobody.

00:05:11.176 --> 00:05:12.878
It's an amazing thing.

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:14.980
-Imagine standing there
and listening to the president

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.782
tell you who dies from a virus

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:18.817
and having it describe you
to a T.

00:05:18.817 --> 00:05:20.352
[ As Trump ]
It affects old people.

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:22.555
Old people with heart issues,
maybe diabetes, you know,

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:26.459
people who gather together
in large groups without a mask.

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:28.660
They're certainly in
the danger zone.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.429
[ Normal voice ]
Must be such a weird drive home.

00:05:30.429 --> 00:05:33.031
"Hey, honey, you think
my pacemaker

00:05:33.031 --> 00:05:35.301
counts as a heart issue?"

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:36.702
But, yeah, man,
it's an amazing thing

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:38.671
that nobody's really affected
by this deadly

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.172
and highly contagious virus.

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:42.442
I'm sure all those people died
just to make you look bad.

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:45.144
I heard they were deep state
Antifa terrorists

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.412
paid for by George Soros
to stop breathing.

00:05:47.412 --> 00:05:48.647
They're probably not even dead.

00:05:48.647 --> 00:05:50.917
They're probably all hanging out
on Antifa Island

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:53.118
talking about how much they love
socialism and fake news.

00:05:53.118 --> 00:05:55.721
The President is
a deeply sick man.

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:57.155
Usually when you hear
someone talk like that,

00:05:57.155 --> 00:05:58.891
they're being fitted
for a Hannibal Lecter mask

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:01.026
or holding a sign
in Times Square.

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:02.861
Coronavirus isn't real.
De Blasio is an alien.

00:06:02.861 --> 00:06:03.929
The moon is following me.

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:05.698
Every time I turn around,
it's there.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.666
COVID is currently
the third highest

00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:08.834
cause of death in the U.S.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:10.069
200,000 people have died.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:12.405
Many more could die
in the coming months.

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:15.007
And the President is out there
telling people six months in

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.642
that virtually
nobody's affected.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:19.979
Just because you're not affected
doesn't mean nobody's affected.

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:22.081
You're safe because
you and everyone around you

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:24.517
get tested every day and you get
the results back instantly.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.418
Meanwhile, regular people
had to wait in their cars

00:06:26.418 --> 00:06:28.854
for hours like they were
lined up at a toll booth

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:30.589
trying to leave New Jersey
during the third quarter

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:32.558
of a Jets game or Giants game.

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:36.963
They're both bad at football.

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.397
I say that risking the fact

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:42.068
that the Giants are the team
all the security guards like.

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:45.137
Also, one more thing,
it's not true

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:46.939
the coronavirus only affects
the elderly

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:48.641
and people
with pre-existing conditions.

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:51.176
But even if it were,
that's like half the population.

00:06:51.176 --> 00:06:53.345
It's like if an ax murderer
was on the loose

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:54.713
and the cops were like,
"Don't worry.

00:06:54.713 --> 00:06:56.949
It only affects
sexy teens taking showers."

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:59.551
And Trump knows better.
He knows better.

00:06:59.551 --> 00:07:02.421
Remember, he told journalist
Bob Woodward

00:07:02.421 --> 00:07:03.889
in those taped conversations

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:07.259
that the coronavirus is actually
very infectious and very deadly

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:08.727
and didn't just affect
the elderly.

00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:10.596
In fact, he went out of his way

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.899
to say young people
could get sick, too.

00:07:51.169 --> 00:07:53.371
It's amazing how different
he sounds in private

00:07:53.371 --> 00:07:55.575
when he wants to impress someone
he thinks is important.

00:07:55.575 --> 00:07:58.177
It's like seeing Larry the
Cable Guy in a fancy restaurant

00:07:58.177 --> 00:08:00.947
wearing sleeves and
holding forth on wine varietals.

00:08:00.947 --> 00:08:03.248
Trump almost sounds normal.

00:08:03.248 --> 00:08:05.984
It's like a local news story
where a guy gets hit on the head

00:08:05.984 --> 00:08:07.653
with a paint can
and becomes a genius,

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:10.189
except Trump probably got hit
in the head with a golf ball

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:11.724
after shanking it in the woods

00:08:11.724 --> 00:08:13.459
and ricocheting it off a tree.

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:15.561
[ As Trump ]
Coronavirus is a hoax.

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:18.363
On the other hand,
I did read a double-blind,

00:08:18.363 --> 00:08:21.067
peer-reviewed clinical study
that suggests aerosols

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:24.303
are a more concerning vector
than fomites.

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:26.005
Did I say fomites?
I meant...

00:08:26.005 --> 00:08:27.506
-Yosemites.

00:08:27.506 --> 00:08:29.341
-Remember?

00:08:29.341 --> 00:08:31.544
We forget,
but that also happened.

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:32.912
Hearing Trump
on the Woodward tapes

00:08:32.912 --> 00:08:34.813
is like seeing
the original Homer Simpson.

00:08:34.813 --> 00:08:36.982
It's a completely
different person.

00:08:36.982 --> 00:08:38.150
That's Homer?

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.118
I thought that was
Walter Matthau.

00:08:40.118 --> 00:08:42.054
[ Laughs ]

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:45.290
Sal Gentile writes some
trenchant political commentary,

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:49.195
but he also got that old
Homer joke in.

00:08:49.195 --> 00:08:52.164
So we know that Trump is at
least capable of understanding

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:53.598
the deadly reality of the virus,

00:08:53.598 --> 00:08:56.501
which makes his lies about it
all the more psychotic

00:08:56.501 --> 00:08:57.536
and criminally negligent.

00:08:57.536 --> 00:08:59.071
He knows people will die,

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:01.307
and he's telling them
not to worry anyway.

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:02.641
He's President Big Tobacco.

00:09:02.641 --> 00:09:05.578
Anyone else doing that
would get sued or go to jail.

00:09:05.578 --> 00:09:07.212
If an auto manufacturer

00:09:07.212 --> 00:09:09.081
told people their car
was perfectly safe

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:11.617
even though they knew
there were no airbags

00:09:11.617 --> 00:09:13.652
and the brakes were 50/50,
they'd get in trouble.

00:09:13.652 --> 00:09:15.988
Of course, if they just
called it a Maga-rati,

00:09:15.988 --> 00:09:17.823
40% of the country
would rush to buy it

00:09:17.823 --> 00:09:20.292
so they could own the libs
by driving off Freedom Cliff.

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:22.562
The simple fact is
that sane people

00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:24.130
who've spend any amount of time
with him

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:26.398
know Trump is a deeply
disturbed individual

00:09:26.398 --> 00:09:28.000
with no regard for human life,

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.803
who doesn't care about anyone
or anything

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:32.471
unless it can enrich
or empower him.

00:09:32.471 --> 00:09:34.706
We keep hearing that same story
over and over

00:09:34.706 --> 00:09:36.041
from people who worked for him,

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:38.443
quit, and called him
unfit for office after leaving.

00:09:38.443 --> 00:09:40.012
Every three days,
there's another book

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:42.048
by a former
administration official,

00:09:42.048 --> 00:09:43.449
and not one of them
has been titled

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:45.951 line:0%
"He Was Very Nice
&amp; That Was Fine."

00:09:45.951 --> 00:09:48.621
I mean, think about
how many people have left

00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:50.589
Trump's inner circle
or his administration

00:09:50.589 --> 00:09:52.123
and basically said
he's a sociopath

00:09:52.123 --> 00:09:53.559
who's incapable
of doing the job.

00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:56.461
It can't be a coincidence that
all these people worked with him

00:09:56.461 --> 00:09:57.896
and now hate his guts.

00:09:57.896 --> 00:09:59.231
Like, if you were a manager
at Best Buy

00:09:59.231 --> 00:10:01.433
and 50 --
50 of your employees quit

00:10:01.433 --> 00:10:04.303
and they all said it's
'cause the new guy, Brad,

00:10:04.303 --> 00:10:05.771
kept putting pictures
of his butthole

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:08.073
up on the 4K ultra HD TVs,

00:10:08.073 --> 00:10:10.008
your reaction wouldn't be like,
"Well, I guess they're leaving

00:10:10.008 --> 00:10:11.877
'cause they're Walmart fans."

00:10:11.877 --> 00:10:13.312
Take, for example, Olivia Troye,

00:10:13.312 --> 00:10:15.281
former adviser
to Vice President Mike Pence,

00:10:15.281 --> 00:10:16.948
who worked on
the coronavirus task force.

00:10:16.948 --> 00:10:19.084
In a recent ad for Biden,

00:10:19.084 --> 00:10:21.153
Troye explained that she quit
because Trump didn't care

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:22.588
if people died from the virus,

00:10:22.588 --> 00:10:25.023
including -- including
his own supporters.

00:10:25.023 --> 00:10:27.526
-The truth is,
he doesn't actually care

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.795
about anyone else but himself.

00:10:29.795 --> 00:10:31.930
He made a statement once.
It was very striking.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:35.167
I never forgot it because it
pretty much defined who he was.

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:37.002
When we were
in a task force meeting,

00:10:37.002 --> 00:10:39.138
President said, "Maybe this
COVID thing is a good thing.

00:10:39.138 --> 00:10:40.639
I don't like shaking hands
with people.

00:10:40.639 --> 00:10:44.143
I don't have to shake hands
with these disgusting people."

00:10:44.143 --> 00:10:46.245
Those disgusting people
are the same people

00:10:46.245 --> 00:10:47.847
that he claims to care about.

00:10:47.847 --> 00:10:50.049
These are the people
still going to his rallies today

00:10:50.049 --> 00:10:53.185
who have complete faith
in who he is.

00:10:53.185 --> 00:10:55.487
-I'm surprised Trump ever shook
hands with his supporters.

00:10:55.487 --> 00:10:58.391
He's a wealthy germophobe
who lived in a golden penthouse

00:10:58.391 --> 00:10:59.758
and traveled everywhere by limo.

00:10:59.758 --> 00:11:01.259
Of course he was disgusted

00:11:01.259 --> 00:11:03.195
by interacting with normal,
non-rich people.

00:11:03.195 --> 00:11:05.998
Even before the pandemic,
he probably finished his rallies

00:11:05.998 --> 00:11:08.934
and then sent Mike Pence out to
shake hands in a Trump disguise.

00:11:08.934 --> 00:11:11.303
[ As Pence ] I really don't want
to do this, sir.

00:11:11.303 --> 00:11:13.071
[ As Trump ] Then maybe you
shouldn't have been so stingy

00:11:13.071 --> 00:11:15.107
with your kisses.

00:11:15.107 --> 00:11:17.509
Maybe you're starting
to regret that choice now.

00:11:17.509 --> 00:11:19.678
[ Normal voice ] Republicans
are in lockstep behind this guy,

00:11:19.678 --> 00:11:22.081
all so they can win
and maintain power.

00:11:22.081 --> 00:11:23.916
That's the corrupt bargain
they've made --

00:11:23.916 --> 00:11:26.485
back an unrepentant
criminal sociopath

00:11:26.485 --> 00:11:27.919
who's overseen
the preventable deaths

00:11:27.919 --> 00:11:29.388
of hundreds of thousands
of Americans.

00:11:29.388 --> 00:11:32.190
And in return, they get
a conservative super majority

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:34.292
on the Supreme Court that could
destroy Obamacare,

00:11:34.292 --> 00:11:36.529
rip up Roe v. Wade,
and invalidate the results

00:11:36.529 --> 00:11:38.230
of the November election
if Trump loses.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:39.231
That's their plan.

00:11:39.231 --> 00:11:40.999
They do not care
about the pandemic.

00:11:40.999 --> 00:11:43.402
Inside the Trump White House
and the Republican Party,

00:11:43.402 --> 00:11:44.469
the COVID death toll...

00:11:44.469 --> 00:11:47.339
-Affects virtually nobody.

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:49.075
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:52.445 --> 00:11:53.913
God's Love We Deliver cooks

00:11:53.913 --> 00:11:56.015
and brings over two million
meals a year to men,

00:11:56.015 --> 00:11:58.584
women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:11:58.584 --> 00:12:00.419
cancer,
and other serious illnesses,

00:12:00.419 --> 00:12:02.020
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.790
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the "donate" button.

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.625
Stay safe.
Wash your hands.

00:12:06.625 --> 00:12:08.728
Wear a mask.
We love you.

